   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Understanding migration dynamics between Uzbekistan and Sweden Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is dedicated to improving the understanding of migration and mobility dynamics between Uzbekistan and Sweden by conducting detailed research. It will delve into the reasons behind migration, mobility patterns, emerging trends, the intent to move, experiences during the journey, encountered challenges, specific vulnerabilities (including gender-related issues), protection requirements, and information accessibility. This project will engage specialists and utilize proven tools and methods to fill in research gaps identified in the preliminary phase that took place from 1 October to 31 December 2023. Over the course of this seven-month endeavor, IOM&apos;s activities will include outreach, interviews with key informants, digital and face-to-face surveys, discussions within focus groups, among other investigatory actions. This will culminate in the collection and examination of data from previously identified partners and directly from migrants and their communities in both Sweden and Uzbekistan. The two outreach strategies created in the initial phase are key to engaging government bodies, NGOs, diaspora groups, academic circles, migrants, returnees, and their communities in both countries. These strategies will aid in gathering information and data crucial for thorough analysis and reporting within the scope of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
